{
  "$comment": "ethers v5 and v6 (#52): a JsonRpcProvider sends JSON-RPC to the URL it is built with. A BrowserProvider (v5 Web3Provider) talks to the wallet and a WebSocketProvider over a socket: calls through them are not HTTP requests of the app. `rpc` is the method on the wire. A node vendor's provider (`InfuraProvider`, `AlchemyProvider`, `QuickNodeProvider`, #78) builds its URL from the network, as the `hosts` copied from ethers 6.13 and 5.7 say; `getDefaultProvider(url)` is a JsonRpcProvider, with a network name it spreads requests over several vendors. A Contract (#78) sends what its runner can: a provider only reads (`eth_call`), a Wallet signs in the app (`eth_sendRawTransaction`), `provider.getSigner()` has the node sign (`eth_sendTransaction`); a function called directly is a view or a transaction as the ABI written in the code says, either when it does not. `*` in a key is one of the ABI's functions, never one of `notFunctions`.",
